```
Title: Potential Persistence Via MyComputer Registry Keys
Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
Date: 2022-08-09
Level: high
Description: Detects modification to the "Default" value of the "MyComputer" key and subkeys to point to a custom binary that will be launched whenever the associated action is executed (see reference section for example)
MITRE Tactic: Persistence
Tags: attack.persistence
Reference: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_persistence_mycomputer.yml
 False Positives:
   - Unlikely but if you experience FPs add specific processes and locations you would like to monitor for
```
TargetObject="*\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Explorer\\MyComputer*" TargetObject="*path\\(Default)" NOT (Details IN ("%%SystemRoot%%\\*", "%%Windir%%\\*", "%SystemRoot%\\*", "%Windir%\\*", "C:\\Windows\\*") (Details IN ("*\\System32\\sdclt.exe", "*\\SysWOW64\\sdclt.exe") TargetObject="*\\MyComputer\\BackupPath\\(Default)") OR (Details IN ("*\\System32\\cleanmgr.exe /D %c", "*\\SysWOW64\\cleanmgr.exe /D %c", "*\\System32\\cleanmgr.exe /D %%c", "*\\SysWOW64\\cleanmgr.exe /D %%c") TargetObject="*\\MyComputer\\cleanuppath\\(Default)") OR (Details IN ("*\\System32\\dfrgui.exe", "*\\SysWOW64\\dfrgui.exe") TargetObject="*\\MyComputer\\DefragPath\\(Default)"))